items.prompt:
Let $X\sim\operatorname{Bernoulli}(0.1)$ and use Hamming distortion.

Compare two zero-rate decoders:


1. always output $\widehat X=0$;

2. independently sample $\widehat X\sim\operatorname{Bernoulli}(0.1)$.

For each decoder, compute:

- expected distortion;
- the reconstruction marginal;
- whether perfect perception $P_{\widehat X}=P_X$ holds.

Explain the cost of the perception constraint.
